\[\left(\begin{array}{ccc}u&u\\ u&t\end{array}\right)^{-1}=\frac{1}{t-u}\left(\begin{array}{ccc}t/u&-1\\ -1&1\end{array}\right).\]

In particular, the conditional mean (3.7) is obtained by linearly interpolating between \((u,x)\) and \((t,y)\).

