\[\tilde{W}_{i}(t)=\frac{W_{i}(t)-\bar{W}(t)}{s(t)/\sqrt{t}}, \tag{4.64}\]

with \(s(t)\) the sample standard deviation of \(W_{1}(t),\ldots,W_{n}(t)\), matches both first and second moments. But for this it seems preferable to scale the increments of the Brownian motion: with

\[W_{i}(t_{k})=\sum_{j=1}^{k}\sqrt{t_{j}-t_{j-1}}Z_{ij}\]

