##### Commutativity Condition

As noted in Section 6.1.1, the mixed Brownian integrals \(I_{(j,k)}\) with \(j\neq k\) are difficult to simulate, so (6.32) does not provide a practical algorithm without further simplification. Simulation of the mixed integrals is obviated in models satisfying the _commutativity condition_

\[{\cal L}^{k}b_{ij}={\cal L}^{j}b_{ik} \tag{6.33}\]

for all \(i=1,\ldots,d\). This is a rather artificial condition and is not often satisfied in practice, but it provides an interesting simplification of the second-order approximation.

