#### Smoothing

We noted in Section 7.2.2 that discontinuities in a discounted payoff generally make the pathwise method inapplicable. In some cases, this obstacle can be overcome by smoothing discontinuities through conditional expectations. We illustrate this idea with two examples.

Our first example is the discounted digital payoff \(Y=e^{-rT}\mathbf{1}\{S(T)>K\}\), which also arises in the derivative of a standard call option; see Example 7.2.6. If \(S\sim\mbox{GBM}(\mu,\sigma^{2})\) and we fix \(0<\epsilon<T\), then

