Numerical results reported in GHS [143] show that this combination of importance sampling and stratification can substantially reduce variance, especially at values of \(x\) for which \(P(L>x)\) is small. The results in [143] use strata that are equiprobable under the \(\theta\)-twisted distribution, meaning that

\[P_{\theta}(Q\in A_{1})=\cdots=P_{\theta}(Q\in A_{K})=\frac{1}{K},\]

