The specific constructions based on the \(t\) distribution in (9.22) and based on the normal distribution in (9.42) are special cases of the general copula representation in (9.43). If \(F\) is a multivariate normal distribution, \(C_{F}\) in (9.44) is a normal copula and if \(F\) is a multivariate \(t\) distribution, \(C_{F}\) is a \(t\)-copula. These copula functions can then be applied to other marginal distributions to link those marginals using the dependence structure of the multivariate normal or \(t\).

