By choosing \(\theta>0\), we thus increase the probability of default.

Now apply this exponential twist to all the \(Y_{i}\). Because the \(Y_{i}\) are independent, the resulting likelihood ratio is the product of the individual likelihood ratios and is thus given by

\[\prod_{i=1}^{m}\exp(\theta Y_{i}-\psi(\theta))=\exp(\theta L-m\psi(\theta)).\]

