\[P(L>x)=\mathsf{E}_{\theta}\left[e^{-\theta L+m\psi(\theta)}\mathbf{1}\{L>x\}\right] \tag{9.46}\]

for the loss probability. The expression inside the expectation on the right provides an unbiased estimator of the loss probability if sampled under the new 

